      <h1>Bitcoin Node Software Explained</h1>
      <p class="msc-learn-page__deck">Bitcoin node software connects to peers and may validate, relay, store, or serve network data according to its configuration. Different implementations can enforce compatible consensus rules while making different choices about transaction policy, features, interfaces, release processes, and defaults. Choosing software therefore requires more than comparing names or popularity.</p>
      <ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Nodes</li><li>Deep</li><li>Comparison</li><li>19 minutes</li><li>Reviewed 2026-07-18</li></ul>
